Match report V Velocity Cobras
The lads welcomed Velocity Cobras for our first game of the season this morning in what turned out to be a very end to end entertaining game. 
  
The lads started strong with many chances Infront of goal but we failed to get a good attempt on target at first but then soon found our chances being saved by a good Velocity keeper who was brave in the goal all game. 

The first goal came from Velocity after a a foul was given outside the box as we looked to break on the counter after winning the ball back. Velocity took the free kick which took two deflections on the way in to give them the lead. 

HT 0-1 - I asked more from the lads to keep up with intensity of the game, keep passing more and look for our outlets on the wings. A shift in some positions seen us wake up more in midfield and Farra equalised when Kaiden was put on through goal by Joey. 
A bit of momentum with us and the game going either way Velocity broke on a counter to play a ball into the box from a cross that stroke jack's hand ...some say it was harsh and his hand was down by his side in a natural position but no VAR here to overturn this one. 
Penalty taken and was brillianty saved by Finley but unfortunately the rebound gave the lad another chance to follow it up and give them the lead. 
A quick message to the lads to keep going, I felt like we deserved something from this game and a battle in midfield commencing with Louis putting the ball through to Kaiden seen us get the qualiser.

  A few nervy chances towards the end but full time 2-2 which was a brilliant game. To summarise the lads were fantastic today, they battled till the end and got a respective well earned point. 
  
